=== Benjamini-Hochberg, q=0.05 (20 positive claims, p-values derived from the frozen logs at run time, clustered p where available) ===
  [KEEP] p=<1e-16   Extras end within 1 run vs regulation (two-proportion)  (mlb_extras.log [the ghost-runner base rate itself — a fact about baseball, unaffected by the 2026-09-23 retraction above. It is no longer described as the rate 'the cell is mispriced against': on pre-game information the cell is not under-priced at all])
  [KEEP] p=8.7e-14  RETRACTED — MLB extra-inning 1-2-run cell under-priced, BOTH venues  (mlb_extras.log [RETRACTED 2026-09-23 — the p-value is real and the statistic is NOT. `extras` is realized DURING the game, outside the forecaster's information set, so splitting on it breaks the calibration identity mechanically. extras_conditioning.log S1: a CONSTANT at the unconditional base rate scores +21.19pt on the same split and a pre-game-information-only forecast +21.23pt, against the market's +20.22pt — neither can misprice the ghost-runner rule, so the statistic has no power to detect mispricing. The whole published gap IS the extras/margin dependence. Kept in the family so the BH computation is over the claims actually made, not a curated subset; BH still marks it KEEP because its p-value was never the problem])
  [KEEP] p=3.6e-13  Markets beat walk-forward Elo floor  (model_benchmark.log [weakest of the three venue comparisons is quoted])
  [KEEP] p=1.2e-12  Minute-scale bidirectional K<->P predictability  (minute_lead_lag.log)
  [KEEP] p=6e-08    Ladder-cost: selling MLB ladder rungs LOSES money  (ladder_cost.log [uses each contract's own settlement; not a Kalshi-specific bias])
  [KEEP] p=1.1e-07  BOOKS' outright longshots overpriced (0-3mo, cluster-t)  (book_outrights.log [H0: $1 back per $1; t on 19 df — statistically identical to Kalshi's $0.33])
  [KEEP] p=5.7e-07  Exchanges price closer to the books that just updated (Poly)  (book_freshness.log [NEW 2026-09-16. Closing cross-section, so it is PROXIMITY not precedence: an exchange that leads and books that catch up produce the same picture. Economically small — 9% of the fresh-stale price gap. Kalshi's term is the same sign and size (-0.021pt, t=-3.7).])
  [KEEP] p=6.8e-06  Book consensus predicts exchanges' next 5-min move (Poly)  (five_min.log [ZERO in the final 2h, lives in sub-0.5pt book moves, and as strong from a frozen quote — drift alignment, not news transmission])
  [KEEP] p=1.1e-05  Cross-venue 15-min predictability, P->K only  (lead_lag.log [the book->P term this claim once included is now z=-0.1 and retired])
  [KEEP] p=0.00017  Exchanges drift AGAINST an imminent book move (Poly, clean panel)  (book_panel.log [as above; Polymarket's share is the more stable of the two (23%->21% across cleaning)])
  [KEEP] p=0.00031  Poly relative volume falls at the fee date (DiD)  (fee_liquidity.log)
  [KEEP] p=0.001    Late flow predicts beyond the closing book  (late_flow.log)
  [KEEP] p=0.0019   Exchanges drift AGAINST an imminent book move (Kalshi, clean panel)  (book_panel.log [NEW 2026-09-16. The anticipation-share claim was never in this family; registering it was overdue and it enters on the membership-constant population, not the published one. Cleaning the instrument moved the share AWAY from 50% (34%->26%), so the effect is not the averaging artifact it was suspected of being.])
  [KEEP] p=0.0027   MLB 1-2-run cell OVER-priced in extras-prone games (pre-game Z)  (extras_conditioning.log [NEW 2026-09-23, and it is the RETRACTED claim's replacement with the sign reversed. Regressing (realized - implied) on a cross-fitted ex-ante extras propensity — a Z the market could see — gives coef=-1.1495, z=-3.00 date-clustered (-2.89 game-clustered, -2.41 iid), i.e. the market slightly OVER-prices the narrow-margin cell in the games most likely to reach extras. ~4pt swing across the whole propensity range: small, robust to the error structure, and opposite in sign to what the retracted statistic appeared to show. Flagged as specification-search-adjacent: it was found while auditing the retracted claim, not registered in advance])
  [KEEP] p=0.008    Book consensus predicts Poly's next 15-min move, final 2h, constant panel  (book_panel.log [NEW 2026-09-16, and it exists only AFTER the composition noise is removed — the pooled panel shows -0.004 (z=-0.1). Registered as a positive claim because it is one, but the identification cuts in the same log read it as catch-up bookkeeping, not transmission: it lives in RESTING quotes (z=+5.5) not awake ones (z=+1.2), lives in sub-0.5pt drift not news-sized moves, and does NOT sharpen at the 5-min clock (final-2h -0.008, z=-0.1), which is the opposite of a fixed wall-clock lag's signature.])
  [KEEP] p=0.016    Books beat Kalshi ladders as DISTRIBUTIONS (pooled RPS)  (multi_outcome.log [post-convention-fix the edge is NBA-carried and small; MLB n.s.])
  [KEEP] p=0.021    Kalshi encompasses Polymarket at close  (encompassing.log [FRAGILE — survives BH here, but this family has printed 0.004, 0.048, 0.044, 0.054 and 0.021 across five vintages of the same claim: a result at the resolution limit, not a stable effect])
  [KEEP] p=0.033    Kalshi encompasses book at close  (encompassing.log [FRAGILE — same caveat as the K-vs-P term above])
  [drop] p=0.072    Books lead Kalshi at T-24h  (horizon_equivalence.log [softened on the completed 84%-coverage T-24h sample])
  [drop] p=0.13     Murphy sup-t: Kalshi edge vs Shin-de-vigged book  (murphy.log [RETRACTED 2026-09-03 — see the docstring; kept in the family so the BH computation is over the claims actually made, not a curated subset])

